  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rSite and Block Plan BR26-01 Rev001;\rExisting Floor Plans BR26-02 Rev001;\rExisting AA Section Elevations Plans BR26-03 Rev001;\rPlanning Design and Access Statement 03.03.2026\rProposed Floor Plans BR26-04 Rev001;\rProposed AA Section Elevations BR26-05 Rev001;\rHighway Safety Impact form;\rFlood Risk Assessment 30.03.2026;\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans and supporting information, the development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than six residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the cycle parking indicated on drawing \"PROPOSED FLOOR PLANS BR26-04 Rev001\" prior to occupation; unless otherwise agreed; cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ri) Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces one per HMO bedroom.\r\rii) In an accessible location; \r\riii) Secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\riv) Fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r\r\r",
    "Prior to first occupation, the refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
